Fixed HTTP 500 responses for mapped PostgreSQL and MySQL device-interface name, module-interface name, and IP-assignment uniqueness conflicts during API saves, including bulk create and update. These conflicts now return HTTP 400 and roll back the complete operation. Other database errors retain their existing behavior.
Fixed HTTP 500 responses for model validation failures during API saves. Rack relocation errors now identify the affected child device on the location field and roll back the move.
Restored database enforcement of interface-name uniqueness for interfaces attached directly to a device. Names may still repeat across different modules and between device-owned and module-owned interfaces. Bulk API conflicts return HTTP 400 and roll back the operation. The migration stops if existing device-owned duplicates need correction.
Fixed invalid exact MAC-address filters, including negation, returning HTTP 500 instead of HTTP 400. Preserved partial and regular-expression MAC searches, retained the free-text filter widget, and enforced EUI-48 validation.
Fixed malformed IPv4 and IPv6 values in the IP-address `address` filter returning HTTP 500. Invalid values now produce HTTP 400 with a field validation error, including when mixed with valid addresses.
Fixed prefix filters returning server errors or silently ignoring malformed input. Invalid prefixes and nonexistent Prefix UUIDs now produce filter validation errors. Strict prefix filters now report invalid input through filter-form validation.
Fixed available-prefix and available-IP actions failing on invalid request entries, prefix lengths, or address ranges.
Fixed zero and negative limits enumerating all available IP addresses. Zero uses the configured maximum when positive; otherwise zero and negative limits use a finite default count. Malformed limits retain their default fallback.
Fixed malformed regular-expression filters returning server errors instead of filter validation errors in API and web requests.
Fixed bulk component creation reporting success after a database error and committing earlier components when a later component failed form validation. Device and module component creation now roll back the complete batch on failure. Database errors propagate to normal error handling.
